<h2>Bottom Line</h2>
<p>The cost of living in Houston is lower than the national urban average, and housing is the main reason. No state income tax helps too. Budget carefully for the costs that surprise newcomers: property taxes, home and flood insurance, summer electricity and life with one or two cars. Price out a specific neighborhood, get real insurance and utility quotes, and you will know what Houston actually costs for your household. If you are still deciding, start with our guide to <a href="/blog/moving-to-houston/">moving to Houston</a>.</p>
